      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/workflow-state.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Beans and instances are ONE answer, not two",
      "prov:value": "`claim` is drawn only in `Process_BeanOpen`, and `resolve` and `archive` only\nin `Process_BeanClose`; every process that works on a bean calls both (bean\n`m8gz`, `check:bean-calls`). `note` is drawn where the work happens."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/workflow-state.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where running instances live — the state graph on the branch store",
      "prov:value": "Running instances are part of the `beans` graph (`workflow-state` graph typology).\nUnder the state branch architecture (proposal `cat-harness/docs/proposals/state-branch-2026-10-02.md`),\nthe bean graph is mounted from the tip-keyed branch store (`cat/cat-harness/beans`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-02",
        "docs/proposals/state-branch-2026-10-02.md"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/workflow-state.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where running instances live — the state graph on the branch store",
      "prov:value": "Instance ids are **derived from the subject rather than random**, so re-entering\na step finds the instance that is already there. That is not a stylistic\npreference: `beans create` is not idempotent and dedupes on nothing, which\nproduced 14,688 duplicates in one afternoon — 92 % of every open bean in that\nrepo. An id you can recompute is the fix, and it is cheap."
    }
  ]
